# # Reccito API  A receipt management platform that enables businesses to create, manage, and share digital receipts with customers through QR codes, mobile apps, and web interfaces.  ## Key Features  ### 🏢 **Multi-Tenant Architecture** - Organization and store hierarchy - Scoped API access and permissions - Isolated data per organization  ### 📱 **Digital Receipt Management** - Create and store digital receipts - Generate QR codes for easy customer access - Barcode generation for physical receipts - Time-limited QR codes for security  ### 🔐 **Authentication & Security** - API key authentication for merchants - JWT token authentication for customers - Phone-based customer verification with SMS - Rate limiting per organization - Permission-based access control  ## Authentication  ### Merchant Authentication (API Keys) ``` Authorization: Bearer rcp_live_1234567890abcdef ```  Merchants use API keys to access business endpoints. API keys can be scoped to: - **Organization level**: Access to all stores within organization - **Store level**: Access limited to specific store  ## Rate Limits  API requests are rate limited per organization (defaults: 60/minute, 1,000/hour, 10,000/day; configurable per organization). Responses include rate limit headers: - `X-RateLimit-Limit-Minute` / `X-RateLimit-Remaining-Minute` / `X-RateLimit-Reset-Minute` - `X-RateLimit-Limit-Hour` / `X-RateLimit-Remaining-Hour` / `X-RateLimit-Reset-Hour`  ## Error Handling  The API uses standard HTTP status codes. Error responses use one of two shapes depending on the endpoint — integrators should handle both:  - `404` and `500` responses use a structured envelope:   ```json   {       \"error\": {           \"code\": \"NOT_FOUND\",           \"message\": \"The requested resource was not found\",           \"path\": \"/api/v1/merchant/receipts/abc\"       }   }   ``` - All other error responses (400, 401, 403, 422, etc.) use FastAPI's default   `{\"detail\": ...}` shape, where `detail` may be a plain string or a   structured object depending on the endpoint. For example:   ```json   { \"detail\": \"No active subscription found.\" }   ```   or   ```json   { \"detail\": { \"code\": \"free_tier_quota_exceeded\", \"message\": \"...\" } }   ```   `422` validation errors follow FastAPI's standard `detail: [...]` array   shape (field, message, error type per invalid field).  ## Pagination  List endpoints use offset pagination (`page`/`limit` query parameters):  ```json {     \"receipts\": [...],     \"total\": 150,     \"page\": 1,     \"limit\": 25,     \"has_next\": true,     \"has_prev\": false } ```  ## Data Formats  ### Dates and Times Timestamps are ISO 8601. Most are UTC with an explicit offset (`2024-01-15T14:30:00+00:00`); a few older fields may omit the offset — treat any timestamp without one as UTC.  ### Currency and Amounts Monetary amounts are serialized as **decimal strings** (not numbers), with a separate `currency` field. This avoids floating-point precision loss and keeps every money field consistent across the API: ```json {     \"total_amount\": \"12.99\",     \"currency\": \"GBP\" } ``` Request bodies still lenient-accept a JSON number for amounts, but the published contract and every response are string-only.  ### ULIDs Receipt IDs use ULID format for better performance and sortability: ```json \"01HZXYZ123456789ABCD\" ```  ## Support  - **Support**: [dev-support@reccito.com](mailto:dev-support@reccito.com) - **Interactive docs**: [https://api.reccito.com/api/v1/redoc](https://api.reccito.com/api/v1/redoc)    This document covers Reccito's public integrations API. Admin and account-internal operations are not included. 

